  "configuration_id": "config_032",
  "reason": "The current best (config_001: scvi_n200, imagenet_vit_l, transformer, weighted, multiprofile) achieves 0.725 acc. In single-profile, weighted vs concat fusion made almost no difference (0.537 vs 0.532), but that regime is far from the multiprofile performance ceiling. Config_032 is identical to config_001 except fusion=concat, giving a clean single-variable test of whether fusion strategy matters in the high-performing multiprofile+transformer regime. If concat matches weighted, fusion can be treated as a non-critical design dimension, freeing budget to explore image encoder (resnet50) or RNA encoder (pca_n2000) variations. If concat is notably worse, it confirms weighted fusion is a meaningful lever worth preserving. This is the most informative next step because it directly extends the strongest evidence with the minimal possible change, reducing uncertainty about a core design axis before committing further experiments to other dimensions."
}

